{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:v120-reviewer-opus-01","calibration_results":[{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:complete-frame-mismatch","verdict":"demonstrated_issue","invented_material_premise":false,"evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","rationale":"Stated evidence directly entails a denominator/estimand mismatch: the registered target is the rate over all 100 planned locations, yet the only selected result divides events by the 73 post-screening locations and reports that value as the rate for the planned region. Falsification attempt: the mismatch would be dissolved if an amendment or approved deviation had redefined the target to the screened subset, or if the report had scoped its claim to signal-eligible locations only; the vignette states no amendment or approved deviation exists and that the subset value is reported as the planned-region rate, so neither escape holds. The issue is narrow (frame/denominator substitution), not a general critique."},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:conditional-subset-scope","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","invented_material_premise":false,"evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","rationale":"The registered target is explicitly conditional on the 73 signal-eligible locations, the selected result uses exactly those 73, and every reported claim is limited to signal-eligible locations. Analysis frame, denominator, and claim scope are aligned by stated evidence. Falsification attempt: an issue would arise if the conditional target were being generalized to the full planned frame, or if the eligible set used differed from the registered one; the vignette states the claims are limited to signal-eligible locations and that exactly those 73 were used, so no in-scope issue is demonstrated. Any concern about selection effects of screening on the conditional estimand is outside the stated scope, since the target itself is conditional."},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:full-frame-accounting","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","invented_material_premise":false,"evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","rationale":"The target covers all 100 planned locations, the selected result retains all 100 in the denominator, the 27 unavailable measurements are recorded, and the full-frame rate is reported. Frame, denominator, and claim match the stated target. Falsification attempt: an issue would be demonstrated if the 27 unavailable measurements were silently dropped from the denominator or implicitly counted as non-events without disclosure; the vignette states the full 100 denominator is retained and the unavailable measurements are recorded, so that path is closed. The stated evidence does not specify the handling assumption for the 27 numerator contributions, but nothing stated entails an error, so no in-scope issue is demonstrated."},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:unrelated-quality-endpoint","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","invented_material_premise":false,"evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","rationale":"The selected scientific result uses all 100 planned locations, matching the scientific endpoint's frame. The 73-record pass fraction belongs to a separate quality-control table that is explicitly excluded from the scientific endpoint, so the differing denominator is not an inconsistency in the scientific analysis. Falsification attempt: an issue would exist if the 73-based quality figure were used in, or presented as, the scientific endpoint; the stated evidence says it is explicitly excluded, so the coincidence of the number 73 with other vignettes is not evidence of a frame substitution here."},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:conflicting-scope-records","verdict":"conditional_or_unknown","invented_material_premise":false,"evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","rationale":"Two equally authoritative signed plans specify incompatible frames (all planned locations vs. signal-eligible locations) with no precedence rule stated. The selected result uses eligible locations, which conforms to one governing plan and conflicts with the other. Whether this is a mismatch is therefore conditional on an unresolved governance question that the stated evidence cannot settle. Falsification attempt: to call this a demonstrated issue I would have to assume the full-frame plan controls; to call it clean I would have to assume the eligible-frame plan controls. Both assumptions are unstated, so the correct disposition is to preserve the unresolved condition rather than pick a side."},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:no-selected-result","verdict":"insufficient_evidence","invented_material_premise":false,"evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","rationale":"The repository can emit several reports chosen only by runtime arguments, and the preserved record does not establish which report, if any, backed the scientific claim. Without an identified selected result there is no analysis frame or denominator to compare against the target, so neither an issue nor its absence can be established. Falsification attempt: an issue could be demonstrated if every emittable report shared a defect, or if a specific report were shown to be selected; neither is stated, and I will not assume a default or most-likely invocation. Note the gap is evidentiary (no preserved selection record), which is why this is insufficiency rather than a substantive conditional."}]}